.TH LIBEX\-CORE 1 "" "libex\-core" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
libex\-core \- fetch Audible metadata
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B libex\-core
[\fIOPTION\fR]... \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGUMENT\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Fetch Audible metadata. Results are written to standard output as JSON, and logs and errors go to standard error.
.SH OPTIONS
Options precede the command.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
show this help message and exit
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR
show the version number and exit
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
print only the final error line
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
more detail on standard error, repeat as \-vv for debug output with tracebacks
.SH COMMANDS
.SS book get
\fBlibex\-core book get\fR \fIASIN\fR
.PP
Print one book as JSON. Exits 3 when Audible has no such book.
.TP
\fIASIN\fR
ASIN of the book
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
show this help message and exit
.TP
\fB\-\-region\fR
the Audible marketplace to ask, default us
.SS book bulk
\fBlibex\-core book bulk\fR \fIASIN\fR
.PP
Print up to 1000 books as JSON, with the ASINs that were not found, were only placeholders, or could not be fetched listed beside them. ASINs may be given as arguments, in a file, or both, separated by commas or white space. The books can be filtered and sorted. A result that is only partly complete is still printed and the status is 0.
.TP
\fIASIN\fR
ASIN of a book, repeat for more
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
show this help message and exit
.TP
\fB\-\-file\fR
read more ASINs from this file, or from standard input when it is \-
.TP
\fB\-\-region\fR
the Audible marketplace to ask, default us
.TP
\fB\-\-language\fR
Filter by language (exact match)
.TP
\fB\-\-book\-format\fR
Filter by book format (e.g. unabridged)
.TP
\fB\-\-explicit\fR
Filter by explicit
.TP
\fB\-\-whisper\-sync\fR
Filter by Whispersync availability
.TP
\fB\-\-has\-pdf\fR
Filter by PDF companion availability
.TP
\fB\-\-is\-vvab\fR
Filter by VVAB (virtual voice audiobook) status
.TP
\fB\-\-plan\-name\fR
Filter by Audible plan name (e.g. US Minerva)
.TP
\fB\-\-rating\-better\-than\fR
Minimum rating
.TP
\fB\-\-rating\-worse\-than\fR
Maximum rating
.TP
\fB\-\-longer\-than\fR
Minimum length in minutes
.TP
\fB\-\-shorter\-than\fR
Maximum length in minutes
.TP
\fB\-\-genre\fR
Filter by genre or tag name (partial match, e.g. fantasy)
.TP
\fB\-\-sort\fR
sort the books by this field, default is the order they were found in
.TP
\fB\-\-order\fR
the direction of \-\-sort, default asc
.SS book chapters
\fBlibex\-core book chapters\fR \fIASIN\fR
.PP
Print a book's chapters as JSON. Exits 3 when there is no chapter list, which is true of many records.
.TP
\fIASIN\fR
ASIN of the book
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
show this help message and exit
.TP
\fB\-\-region\fR
the Audible marketplace to ask, default us
.SS book sku
\fBlibex\-core book sku\fR \fISKU\fR
.PP
Print every stored book of a SKU group as JSON, usually the same title in several marketplaces. This is answered from the local store alone, which is off unless LIBEX_CORE_STORAGE is set, and makes no request to Audible. Exits 3 when the store holds none and 5 when storage is off or not ready.
.TP
\fISKU\fR
SKU group identifier
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
show this help message and exit
.SS series get
\fBlibex\-core series get\fR \fIASIN\fR
.PP
Print the series record as JSON. Exits 3 when Audible has no such series.
